comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T20:16:32.214Z",pi-agent,"Duplicate audit found GitHub issue 50. Existing item pm-graph-of5p covers it, so the dry-run planned 0 new items and 1 update; the atomic import applied 0 new items and 1 update."
  "2026-08-28T21:08:54.946Z",pi-agent,"Re-verified sync: pm github import --state all applied 0 creates and 1 update (pm-graph-of5p updated_at refresh). pm duplicates count 0, pm health --strict-exit exit 0."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T20:16:32.810Z",pi-agent,"The first documented install attempt failed under pinned pm 2026.8.22 because npm 12 emits object-shaped npm pack JSON and the installer treated the final } as a tarball name. Pinning @unbrained/pm-cli to 2026.8.28 did not remove the npm-client mismatch, so the verified install uses a temporary npm 10.9.3 path. The published pm-github 2026.8.18 manifest also carried an obsolete pm key and floor 2026.8.3; the workflow removes that key and restores the source floor 2026.8.20 before strict health."
files[6]{path,scope,note}:
  .agents/pm/extensions/.managed-extensions.json,project,Declare pm-github as a project-scoped managed extension.
  .github/workflows/ci.yml,project,CI installs and normalizes the project pm-github extension before health.
  .github/workflows/pm-github-sync.yml,project,Scheduled import runs on automation/pm-github-sync and opens or updates a PR.
  .gitignore,project,Track the managed project extension registry while ignoring extracted artifacts.
  package-lock.json,project,Lock the verified pm CLI version.
  package.json,project,Pin the pm CLI used by the integration.
tests[2]{command,path,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref},note}:
